		{
			"to": "food/malthus",
			"why": "The Origin calls the struggle for existence \"the doctrine of Malthus applied with manifold force to the whole animal and vegetable kingdoms\": Malthus's essay of 1798 is the third step of Darwin's argument."
		},
		{
			"to": "biology/aristotle-animals",
			"why": "By 1866 the Origin's historical sketch opened with a footnote on Aristotle, in whose Physics Darwin read natural selection \"shadowed forth\"; Aristotle's zoology is where this subject begins."
		}
